# VaultCloud — Trivy Accepted Risk File
# These CVEs are in the Debian OS layer of the distroless base image
# (gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian13:nonroot). They are NOT reachable
# by VaultCloud application code. Fixes depend on upstream Google/Debian
# security updates to the base image.
#
# Last updated: 2026-09-16
# Scanner: Trivy v0.74.0
# Base image: gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian13:nonroot (Debian 13.7)

# libexpat1 — XML parser library
# Reachability: LOW — VaultCloud does not parse XML. Expat is a transitive
# dependency of Python's xml.parsers.expat, not imported by app.py.
CVE-2026-66046
CVE-2026-76956
CVE-2026-76957

# libncursesw6 / libtinfo6 — Terminal UI libraries
# Reachability: NONE — Distroless has no shell, no terminal, no ncurses
# binaries. Libraries present as transitive deps, never loaded/executed.
CVE-2025-69720

# libpython3.13 / python3.13-minimal / python3.13-venv
# Reachability: LOW — Affect html.parser, xml.etree, tarfile modules.
# VaultCloud only uses flask, sqlite3, hashlib, logging, os.
CVE-2026-15308
CVE-2026-7210
CVE-2026-82049

# libuuid1 — util-linux UUID library
# Reachability: NONE — CVEs affect mount helpers (mount, nsenter) and
# cgroup tools. Distroless has no shell, no mount utilities.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

